\f0\b\fs48 \cf0 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 GASW Ads Reporter \'97 Internal Tool Documentation\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\fs24 \cf0 Company:
\f1\b0  GA Suit Warehouse (menswear retail, Georgia, USA)\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Website:
\f1\b0  www.gasuitwarehouse.com\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Document date:
\f1\b0  July 16, 2026\uc0\u8232 
\f0\b Tool type:
\f1\b0  Internal-use command-line utility (not distributed to third parties)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 1. Overview\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 GASW Ads Reporter is an internal command-line tool used by GA Suit Warehouse to report on and manage advertising in our own Google Ads account. GA Suit Warehouse is a brick-and-mortar suit retailer; our website generates booked fitting appointments, and Google Ads is our primary paid acquisition channel.\
The tool is used exclusively by the business owner on our own Google Ads account, accessed through our own manager account. It is not a commercial product, is not offered to any third party, and manages no accounts other than our own.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 2. Business model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Our business model is retail: we sell suits and formalwear in our physical store. We do not sell software, advertising services, or API access. The Google Ads API is used solely to operate our own advertising more effectively.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 3. Intended audience\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Internal use only. The sole user is the business owner. The tool runs locally on the owner's computer; there is no hosted service, no user sign-up, and no third-party access of any kind.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 4. Functionality\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 4.1 Reporting (primary use)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Campaign performance reports: cost, clicks, impressions, conversions, conversion value, by day/week/month.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Search terms reports for our Performance Max and Search campaigns, used to identify wasted spend.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Conversion action reports (booked appointments) to measure return on ad spend.\
\ls1\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Asset group / ad performance summaries.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Reports are retrieved with the GoogleAdsService search interface (GAQL queries) and reviewed locally. Query volume is low: typically a few dozen report queries per week.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 4.2 Campaign management (secondary use, human-approved)\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adding negative keywords identified from search terms reports (CampaignCriterionService / SharedCriterionService).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Adjusting campaign budgets within owner-set limits (CampaignBudgetService).\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Pausing or enabling existing campaigns (CampaignService).\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Every change is staged and shown to the owner for explicit approval before it is submitted through the API. The tool does not create accounts, does not create campaigns autonomously, and does not perform bulk or automated mutations.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 5. Architecture and workflow\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The owner runs the tool from the command line on a local machine.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The tool authenticates via OAuth 2.0 (desktop application flow) using credentials from our own Google Cloud project, with the Google Ads API enabled.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The developer token is issued under our own manager account, which is linked to our single client account.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Reports are fetched via GAQL and summarized for the owner.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Proposed changes (negative keywords, budget adjustments) are listed for review; only owner-approved changes are submitted.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 6. Authentication and security\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 OAuth 2.0 desktop flow; the refresh token, client secret, and developer token are stored in a local configuration file on the owner's machine with restricted file permissions.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Credentials are never embedded in our public website code, never committed to source control, and never shared with third parties.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 API access is limited to our own customer ID under our own manager account.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 7. API usage expectations\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Accounts accessed: 1 (our own), via 1 manager account.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Estimated volume: under 1,000 API operations per day, predominantly read-only reporting.\
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Rate limiting and retry behavior follow the official Google Ads API client library defaults.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 8. Compliance\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The tool complies with the Google Ads API Terms and Required Minimum Functionality expectations applicable to internal, own-account tools. It does not resell API access, does not co-mingle data across accounts (there is only one account), and does not provide advertising services to third parties.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

